    "end": 4.32,
    "text": "why overload the body and makes more sense to space them out? Because you're not overloading"
   },
   {
    "id": "t2",
    "start": 4.32,
    "end": 11.76,
    "text": "the body. A newborn baby is exposed to 2,000 to 6,000 new antigens every day. Antigen is just"
   },
   {
    "id": "t3",
    "start": 11.76,
    "end": 17.52,
    "text": "the fancy scientific term for foreign substance in their food, in the air, on the ground, in the"
   },
   {
    "id": "t4",
    "start": 17.52,
    "end": 22.16,
    "text": "things that they touch and put in their mouths. Meanwhile, in the entire childhood vaccination"
   },
   {
    "id": "t5",
    "start": 22.16,
    "end": 28.56,
    "text": "series, all 18 years, there are less than 200 antigens, less than one tenth of what babies are"
   },
   {
    "id": "t6",
    "start": 28.56,
    "end": 30.72,
    "text": "are exposed to on a daily basis."
   },
   {
    "id": "t7",
    "start": 30.72,
    "end": 33.36,
    "text": "There is zero evidence for any benefit"
   },
   {
    "id": "t8",
    "start": 33.36,
    "end": 35.88,
    "text": "for spacing out or separating vaccinations,"
   },
   {
    "id": "t9",
    "start": 35.88,
    "end": 37.92,
    "text": "which is why they needed an executive order"
   },
   {
    "id": "t10",
    "start": 37.92,
    "end": 39.8,
    "text": "because it wasn't backed by science."
   },
   {
    "id": "t11",
    "start": 39.8,
    "end": 42.28,
    "text": "Leap healthcare to the healthcare professionals."
   }
